1
00:00:04,963 --> 00:00:06,756
Yes?

2
00:00:07,757 --> 00:00:08,925
- We came.
- We came.

3
00:00:09,009 --> 00:00:10,301
What?!

4
00:00:10,385 --> 00:00:12,887
<i>All of us are unemployed,</i>

5
00:00:12,971 --> 00:00:15,807
<i>and on a vacation from life, right?</i>

6
00:00:15,890 --> 00:00:16,891
<i>This way.</i>

7
00:00:16,975 --> 00:00:18,685
<i>What? Someone else is here too?</i>

8
00:00:18,768 --> 00:00:20,311
<i>This is my friend, Tetsuro.</i>

9
00:00:20,395 --> 00:00:22,605
<i>A barbecue needs a man's strength!</i>

10
00:00:22,689 --> 00:00:23,898
Who is this handsome guy?

11
00:00:23,982 --> 00:00:26,693
This is Mr. Nishigami,
who takes care of the villas around here.

12
00:00:26,776 --> 00:00:28,194
Mr. Nishigami!

13
00:00:28,278 --> 00:00:29,863
<i>Grim Reaper.</i>

14
00:00:29,946 --> 00:00:32,824
<i>At the end of summer,</i>
<i>this villa ground will be hit</i>

15
00:00:32,907 --> 00:00:35,201
<i>by a large-scale landslide</i>
<i>disaster due to a typhoon.</i>

16
00:00:35,285 --> 00:00:37,245
<i>Make sure to report the precise increase</i>

17
00:00:37,328 --> 00:00:39,539
<i>or decrease in the number</i>
<i>of casualties when that happens.</i>

18
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:42,500
Is it true that you have a villa
in Tatsumi Town?

19
00:00:43,334 --> 00:00:44,502
Mr. Jin?

20
00:00:44,586 --> 00:00:47,922
Can I go there too?

21
00:01:09,360 --> 00:01:10,987
Mr. Jin, get in!

22
00:01:13,573 --> 00:01:14,491
Open it!

23
00:01:14,574 --> 00:01:16,367
Mr. Ichijo!

24
00:01:19,662 --> 00:01:22,123
Mr. Ichijo! Please give us a comment!

25
00:01:22,207 --> 00:01:24,626
Please tell us about the situation!

26
00:01:27,796 --> 00:01:29,172
Damn, he got away!

27
00:01:29,839 --> 00:01:30,924
Hello?

28
00:01:31,007 --> 00:01:32,759
Is this the <i>Weekly Shuubun</i>?

29
00:01:55,782 --> 00:01:56,783
Hello.

30
00:01:57,367 --> 00:01:59,202
Oh, hello.

31
00:01:59,869 --> 00:02:02,747
I'm collecting firewood.

32
00:02:03,581 --> 00:02:06,126
You're here on vacation, aren't you?

33
00:02:06,835 --> 00:02:08,711
Oh, yes, hello.

34
00:02:08,795 --> 00:02:10,338
Then how about…

35
00:02:11,631 --> 00:02:13,341
doing some fishing?

36
00:02:14,592 --> 00:02:15,760
Fishing?

37
00:02:27,730 --> 00:02:28,940
This is amazing.

38
00:02:29,023 --> 00:02:30,483
It's cold!

39
00:02:31,526 --> 00:02:34,320
We don't have anything
like this in Tokyo. Incredible.

40
00:02:40,201 --> 00:02:42,203
I wonder if I'll catch anything.

41
00:02:42,287 --> 00:02:44,247
I would love to surprise Konta.

42
00:02:48,126 --> 00:02:50,211
I got something! It's biting!

43
00:02:50,879 --> 00:02:51,754
Whoa!

44
00:02:52,630 --> 00:02:53,798
Oh, wow!

45
00:02:55,008 --> 00:02:56,134
Awesome!

46
00:02:57,218 --> 00:02:59,554
I caught one! It's a feisty one!

47
00:02:59,637 --> 00:03:00,847
Just like Konta.

48
00:03:01,639 --> 00:03:03,474
What do I do now…

49
00:03:13,234 --> 00:03:14,068
Fish.

50
00:03:16,738 --> 00:03:19,490
There's a spot nearby
where you can fish for rainbow trout,

51
00:03:19,574 --> 00:03:20,450
so I checked it out.

52
00:03:21,868 --> 00:03:23,828
Oh, fishing…

53
00:03:26,164 --> 00:03:28,124
Are you going to eat those?

54
00:03:28,207 --> 00:03:29,250
Oh, yes.

55
00:03:29,792 --> 00:03:32,462
I'm going to grill them with salt.

56
00:03:33,963 --> 00:03:37,592
So you're having another barbecue today?

57
00:03:37,675 --> 00:03:38,801
Yes.

58
00:03:43,264 --> 00:03:45,725
I am so incredibly bored.

59
00:03:45,808 --> 00:03:46,893
Hey!

60
00:03:46,976 --> 00:03:49,103
- Let's watch this show together.
- What?

61
00:03:49,187 --> 00:03:51,648
It's from a little while ago,
but they say it's really good.

62
00:03:51,731 --> 00:03:52,857
What?

63
00:03:54,484 --> 00:03:57,612
I love the whole "he's-a-terrorist
but-he's-also-a-detective" thing.

64
00:03:57,695 --> 00:03:59,447
Oh, I've seen this actor before.

65
00:03:59,530 --> 00:04:00,406
Hey.

66
00:04:00,490 --> 00:04:02,867
If you two are so bored, help me clean up.

67
00:04:03,493 --> 00:04:06,079
Can't, we're watching a show.

68
00:04:06,663 --> 00:04:07,747
Come on!

69
00:04:10,625 --> 00:04:12,543
I'm back.

70
00:04:12,627 --> 00:04:13,753
Welcome back.

71
00:04:13,836 --> 00:04:15,546
Oh, Mr. Nishigami.

72
00:04:15,630 --> 00:04:17,966
I brought some firewood.

73
00:04:18,049 --> 00:04:18,925
Wait, firewood?

74
00:04:19,008 --> 00:04:20,468
Are we doing another barbecue today?

75
00:04:20,551 --> 00:04:22,512
That's great!

76
00:04:22,595 --> 00:04:24,847
What's in there?

77
00:04:27,892 --> 00:04:30,853
Today's feast.

78
00:04:32,480 --> 00:04:34,857
They're so pretty! Look how they sparkle!

79
00:04:36,818 --> 00:04:37,694
What?

80
00:04:38,278 --> 00:04:39,279
Welcome back.

81
00:04:39,362 --> 00:04:40,363
We're home.

82
00:04:40,446 --> 00:04:41,906
What? Who's this?

83
00:04:41,990 --> 00:04:43,700
Who is this old guy?

84
00:04:44,409 --> 00:04:45,868
What? No way!

85
00:04:45,952 --> 00:04:48,454
It's <i>Terrorist Detective!</i>
It's the guy from <i>Terrorist Detective!</i>

86
00:04:48,538 --> 00:04:49,789
<i>Terrorist Detective</i>, like the…

87
00:04:49,872 --> 00:04:52,083
He's the guy from the show
we were just watching!

88
00:04:52,166 --> 00:04:53,209
Hello.

89
00:04:53,793 --> 00:04:55,253
Wow, it's really him!

90
00:04:55,336 --> 00:04:57,547
Why, how did you end up here, Mr. Jin?

91
00:04:58,589 --> 00:05:00,091
Thanks for your support.

92
00:05:00,675 --> 00:05:03,469
I'm the actor, Jin Ichijo.

93
00:05:06,264 --> 00:05:07,307
Yo!

94
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:39,964
Mr. Jin, come on in!

95
00:05:40,048 --> 00:05:42,216
- Midori, tea! Get some tea!
- Oh, right!

96
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:44,469
Mr. Jin, I'll take your bag.

97
00:05:44,552 --> 00:05:45,470
Hey.

98
00:05:46,137 --> 00:05:47,805
Is it really okay for an old guy like me

99
00:05:47,889 --> 00:05:50,850
to crash with a bunch
of young kids like this?

100
00:05:50,933 --> 00:05:52,769
What are they, students?

101
00:05:52,852 --> 00:05:55,063
No, they're all working adults. Grown-ups!

102
00:05:55,813 --> 00:05:58,316
What about work?
Do they have the day off today?

103
00:05:58,399 --> 00:06:01,903
They're all on an extended le--
Extended brea-- A vacation!

104
00:06:01,986 --> 00:06:03,446
- Take a seat.
- Go ahead.

105
00:06:03,529 --> 00:06:05,073
Hey, why?

106
00:06:05,156 --> 00:06:07,450
Why is a celebrity
coming to a place like this?

107
00:06:07,533 --> 00:06:09,744
Who is that guy again?

108
00:06:09,827 --> 00:06:12,580
It's Jin Ichijo! From <i>Terrorist Detective!</i>

109
00:06:13,873 --> 00:06:16,751
Hey, AI, tell me about Jin Ichijo.

110
00:06:17,251 --> 00:06:20,588
<i>Jin Ichijo is a veteran Japanese actor</i>

111
00:06:20,671 --> 00:06:24,717
<i>known for his compelling</i>
<i>performances and wide range of roles.</i>

112
00:06:24,801 --> 00:06:26,052
We can hear everything, you know!

113
00:06:27,303 --> 00:06:29,847
<i>His notable works include</i>
Terrorist Detective,

114
00:06:29,931 --> 00:06:33,684
Love's End City,<i> and</i>
From a Western Town in a Northern Country.

115
00:06:33,768 --> 00:06:34,727
Right!

116
00:06:34,811 --> 00:06:38,606
I used to watch
<i>Love's End City </i>when I was a kid!

117
00:06:38,689 --> 00:06:39,941
Oh, he's that guy!

118
00:06:40,024 --> 00:06:42,276
The one who played
the main character's boyfriend!

119
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:43,361
I'm sorry.

120
00:06:44,487 --> 00:06:47,281
Sorry to keep you waiting, Mr. Jin.

121
00:06:48,074 --> 00:06:50,451
Here's some tea.

122
00:06:50,535 --> 00:06:51,994
Oh, really?

123
00:06:52,078 --> 00:06:53,955
You watched that?

124
00:06:54,038 --> 00:06:55,540
I watched it with her, too.

125
00:06:56,082 --> 00:06:58,167
This is my younger sister, Midori.

126
00:06:58,751 --> 00:07:00,002
I see.

127
00:07:00,086 --> 00:07:01,546
What a cute little sister.

128
00:07:01,629 --> 00:07:02,547
Mr. Jin!

129
00:07:02,630 --> 00:07:06,968
Look, I was just watching
<i>Terrorist Detective </i>a second ago!

130
00:07:07,051 --> 00:07:09,220
Why are you watching stuff like that?

131
00:07:11,973 --> 00:07:13,182
Well…

132
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:17,311
Allow me to introduce myself properly.

133
00:07:17,895 --> 00:07:19,355
I'm Jin Ichijo.

134
00:07:20,648 --> 00:07:24,735
I apologize for dropping in
so suddenly today.

135
00:07:25,528 --> 00:07:30,950
Thanks to my younger colleague, Konta,
I'll be staying here for a little while.

136
00:07:31,033 --> 00:07:32,660
Nice to meet you all.

137
00:07:33,411 --> 00:07:34,287
Amazing!

138
00:07:34,370 --> 00:07:36,789
He looks picture-perfect
just standing there.

139
00:07:36,873 --> 00:07:38,791
He looks way older than he does on TV.

140
00:07:38,875 --> 00:07:40,710
Hey, watch your mouth.

141
00:07:40,793 --> 00:07:42,128
Don't worry.

142
00:07:42,211 --> 00:07:43,504
It's fine.

143
00:07:44,380 --> 00:07:46,007
She's right.

144
00:07:46,924 --> 00:07:50,845
An old guy like me
is just getting in the way

145
00:07:50,928 --> 00:07:53,764
of you young people having a good time.

146
00:07:53,848 --> 00:07:55,892
You're not in the way at all!

147
00:07:55,975 --> 00:07:59,395
Oh! I want to watch
<i>Terrorist Detective </i>with the actual star

148
00:07:59,479 --> 00:08:01,647
and hear some behind-the-scenes gossip!

149
00:08:01,731 --> 00:08:03,399
Hey, you're being way too pushy!

150
00:08:03,483 --> 00:08:04,609
That's rude.

151
00:08:04,692 --> 00:08:06,944
- You're the rude one, Tsumugi.
- It's fine.

152
00:08:07,487 --> 00:08:08,905
You don't have to be polite with me.

153
00:08:09,489 --> 00:08:11,032
Mind if I watch the Koshien?

154
00:08:11,115 --> 00:08:12,366
Wait, don't turn on the TV!

155
00:08:12,450 --> 00:08:13,534
What?

156
00:08:14,452 --> 00:08:17,955
<i>The famous actor, Jin Ichijo, is involved</i>
<i>in a massive cheating scandal.</i>

157
00:08:18,039 --> 00:08:19,957
<i>Yesterday's issue of the </i>Weekly Shuubun

158
00:08:20,041 --> 00:08:23,669
<i>published a scoop featuring photos of him</i>
<i>on dates with three beautiful women,</i>

159
00:08:23,753 --> 00:08:25,713
<i>causing a massive public uproar.</i>

160
00:08:25,796 --> 00:08:27,131
<i>Mr. Jin really did it this time.</i>

161
00:08:27,215 --> 00:08:31,177
<i>A blonde </i>gyaru<i>, a model-esque beauty,</i>
<i>and on top of that, one with a black bob.</i>

162
00:08:31,260 --> 00:08:32,970
<i>Aren't they a bit too young?</i>

163
00:08:33,054 --> 00:08:34,472
<i>He's a married man, right?</i>

164
00:08:34,555 --> 00:08:37,308
<i>It's pretty shocking</i>
<i>for an actor of his caliber</i>

165
00:08:37,391 --> 00:08:39,393
<i>to be caught in multiple affairs.</i>

166
00:08:43,397 --> 00:08:47,109
It looks like I'm going to have

167
00:08:48,027 --> 00:08:50,029
a much longer break than you all.

168
00:08:50,112 --> 00:08:52,615
Mr. Jin, don't say that, come on!
You're going to be fine!

169
00:08:52,698 --> 00:08:54,408
Mr. Jin, you'll be fine!

170
00:09:01,374 --> 00:09:03,543
You've gotten good at starting fires.

171
00:09:04,335 --> 00:09:06,546
Thanks to your guidance.

172
00:09:08,714 --> 00:09:11,676
By the way, are you from overseas?

173
00:09:11,759 --> 00:09:14,095
The way you talk is just kind of…

174
00:09:15,471 --> 00:09:18,099
Oh, but, if you're from overseas,

175
00:09:18,182 --> 00:09:20,560
it would be strange
to have the last name Nishigami.

176
00:09:20,643 --> 00:09:21,894
Right!

177
00:09:21,978 --> 00:09:24,981
Are you Japanese raised abroad?

178
00:09:27,358 --> 00:09:28,693
I've been…

179
00:09:30,361 --> 00:09:31,946
in this town my whole life.

180
00:09:44,458 --> 00:09:48,671
Hey, how do you even know
that guy in the first place?

181
00:09:48,754 --> 00:09:50,715
Did you tell him to run away
and hide out here

182
00:09:50,798 --> 00:09:52,925
after his affair got exposed
and turned into a scandal?

183
00:09:53,009 --> 00:09:56,596
Mr. Jin took really good care of me
when we worked together.

184
00:09:56,679 --> 00:09:57,638
You worked together?

185
00:09:57,722 --> 00:09:59,181
That's amazing! What role did you play?

186
00:09:59,265 --> 00:10:02,727
Mr. Jin was Nobunaga,
and I was Foot Soldier F.

187
00:10:02,810 --> 00:10:03,686
So you were an extra.

188
00:10:04,770 --> 00:10:07,648
He even took me out for food
after shooting wrapped up.

189
00:10:07,732 --> 00:10:10,359
He's basically like a big brother
to me in the acting world.

190
00:10:10,443 --> 00:10:13,446
For an extra, you sure managed
to win over the guy playing Nobunaga.

191
00:10:13,529 --> 00:10:14,905
Stop saying extra over and over.

192
00:10:14,989 --> 00:10:17,366
Hey, is he staying here tonight?

193
00:10:17,450 --> 00:10:18,993
What are we doing for dinner?

194
00:10:19,076 --> 00:10:21,454
For now, just let him hide out here!

195
00:10:21,537 --> 00:10:23,372
Tokyo is crawling with reporters,
it's dangerous.

196
00:10:23,456 --> 00:10:27,918
Mr. Jin does a lot of commercials, right?
The cancellation penalties must be huge.

197
00:10:28,002 --> 00:10:30,379
Yeah, probably around a hundred
or two hundred million yen.

198
00:10:30,463 --> 00:10:31,922
What? That much?

199
00:10:33,549 --> 00:10:36,677
It feels great out here.

200
00:10:37,553 --> 00:10:41,223
Makes me want a beer.

201
00:10:41,307 --> 00:10:42,183
A beer?

202
00:10:42,266 --> 00:10:45,144
I'll get you one right now.

203
00:10:45,227 --> 00:10:46,729
Mr. Jin, here you go.

204
00:10:46,812 --> 00:10:48,564
- Thank you.
- No prob.

205
00:10:51,651 --> 00:10:55,571
I don't want to give up on health
or that refreshing feel!

206
00:10:55,655 --> 00:10:58,324
For middle-aged people like you!

207
00:10:59,408 --> 00:11:00,368
This…

208
00:11:00,451 --> 00:11:02,787
This is the one I did a commercial for!

209
00:11:02,870 --> 00:11:03,913
I'm sorry.

210
00:11:04,497 --> 00:11:07,875
I'm sure the contract for
this commercial is getting terminated.

211
00:11:07,958 --> 00:11:11,545
And the penalties
are going to be astronomical.

212
00:11:11,629 --> 00:11:13,839
How about some tea instead?

213
00:11:16,550 --> 00:11:20,721
Burning middle-aged fat,
"Body Burning Tea."

214
00:11:20,805 --> 00:11:22,598
Now on sale!

215
00:11:22,681 --> 00:11:25,101
I did the commercial for this one too!

216
00:11:25,184 --> 00:11:26,310
Mr. Jin, calm down!

217
00:11:26,394 --> 00:11:30,773
Here, please,
take a seat in this chair, relax.

218
00:11:30,856 --> 00:11:32,983
I did an advertisement for this too.

219
00:11:33,067 --> 00:11:36,904
The brand ambassador for adult camping.

220
00:11:36,987 --> 00:11:37,863
What?

221
00:11:37,947 --> 00:11:41,367
Oh! Mr. Jin!
Please wipe your tears with these!

222
00:11:46,163 --> 00:11:50,876
Gently embracing your tears with softness.

223
00:11:51,502 --> 00:11:54,046
He really is incredible.
He has commercials for everything.

224
00:11:54,130 --> 00:11:57,174
- I did a commercial for this too.
- That's easily a billion yen right there.

225
00:11:57,258 --> 00:12:00,761
But honestly, I hear they don't usually
demand commercial penalties

226
00:12:00,845 --> 00:12:02,012
just for a suspected affair.

227
00:12:02,096 --> 00:12:04,515
- Really?
- Yes, it's not like he committed a crime.

228
00:12:04,598 --> 00:12:05,474
True.

229
00:12:05,558 --> 00:12:08,602
Still, things are going to be tough
for him as an actor from now on.

230
00:12:08,686 --> 00:12:11,480
That's true. He played many roles
with a strong sense of justice.

231
00:12:11,564 --> 00:12:14,942
Why would he even have an affair
when he has a wife?

232
00:12:15,025 --> 00:12:17,194
- What an absolute piece of garbage.
- Yeah.

233
00:12:17,278 --> 00:12:19,655
There's nowhere left
for him to go but hell.

234
00:12:19,738 --> 00:12:21,115
You guys are pretty harsh.

235
00:12:24,368 --> 00:12:26,036
Thank you for the firewood.

236
00:12:28,164 --> 00:12:29,707
Who is that gentleman?

237
00:12:29,790 --> 00:12:32,793
Oh, he's a famous actor.

238
00:12:32,877 --> 00:12:35,087
He appears in TV shows a lot.

239
00:12:35,171 --> 00:12:38,799
I used to watch
<i>From a Western Town in a Northern Country.</i>

240
00:12:39,592 --> 00:12:40,509
Listen up, Mr. Jin,

241
00:12:40,593 --> 00:12:44,013
I'm just going to say it,
but you brought this entirely on yourself!

242
00:12:44,096 --> 00:12:45,389
Hey, Midori.

243
00:12:45,473 --> 00:12:48,184
It's a hundred times harder on your wife.
She's crying more than you.

244
00:12:48,809 --> 00:12:50,352
And with three women on top of that.

245
00:12:50,436 --> 00:12:52,980
All those women
you cheated with are hurting too.

246
00:12:53,063 --> 00:12:55,232
That's right! You tell him, Midori!

247
00:12:55,316 --> 00:12:56,692
Stop it, Midori!

248
00:12:57,401 --> 00:12:58,694
No!

249
00:13:00,571 --> 00:13:02,198
I didn't do it.

250
00:13:04,408 --> 00:13:06,118
I even denied the affairs

251
00:13:07,745 --> 00:13:10,247
through my agency.

252
00:13:11,790 --> 00:13:13,250
But the media

253
00:13:13,334 --> 00:13:17,379
just made up their minds
based on those photos.

254
00:13:19,048 --> 00:13:20,549
Do you have any idea?

255
00:13:21,926 --> 00:13:27,056
The <i>Weekly Shuubun</i> doesn't care
if they get sued for writing lies.

256
00:13:28,474 --> 00:13:29,517
Why?

257
00:13:30,100 --> 00:13:31,727
Because even if they lose,

258
00:13:31,810 --> 00:13:34,772
the damages are
a measly three million yen.

259
00:13:35,981 --> 00:13:37,358
So they write

260
00:13:38,734 --> 00:13:41,654
whatever lies sell magazines,
and that's all that matters to them.

261
00:13:44,156 --> 00:13:48,911
To people making
hundreds of millions off of fabrications,

262
00:13:50,287 --> 00:13:54,792
a lawsuit is nothing but a scratch.

263
00:13:56,669 --> 00:13:57,920
Meanwhile,

264
00:13:58,712 --> 00:14:02,299
because of that article,
they've stopped shooting my show.

265
00:14:03,592 --> 00:14:08,514
The movie wrap party
was targeted by reporters,

266
00:14:09,473 --> 00:14:15,646
and it has caused trouble
for my agency and other actors.

267
00:14:16,897 --> 00:14:18,774
This isn't anything new.

268
00:14:20,150 --> 00:14:22,194
But we celebrities

269
00:14:23,279 --> 00:14:27,825
are constantly getting screwed over
by their money-making schemes.

270
00:14:30,703 --> 00:14:33,873
Constantly screwed over.

271
00:14:35,583 --> 00:14:39,420
He really is so photogenic, so handsome!

272
00:14:40,045 --> 00:14:44,008
Rinrin, you really don't have a specific
type when it comes to guys, do you?

273
00:14:44,091 --> 00:14:48,888
But, you know, I do feel a little bit
sorry for him looking at this.

274
00:14:48,971 --> 00:14:51,807
I WON'T WATCH HIS DRAMAS ANYMORE
HE'S OVER LOL

275
00:14:51,891 --> 00:14:53,517
WELL DONE SHUUBUN!

276
00:14:54,602 --> 00:14:56,687
I believe you, Mr. Jin.

277
00:14:57,354 --> 00:15:00,065
If it's for your sake,
I don't care if I get dragged too.

278
00:15:00,149 --> 00:15:02,026
Or if they write an article like,

279
00:15:02,109 --> 00:15:05,195
"Why is the rising star Konta
harboring a scumbag cheater actor?"

280
00:15:05,279 --> 00:15:06,572
Hey!

281
00:15:07,406 --> 00:15:10,784
We live in a terrible era.

282
00:15:11,577 --> 00:15:15,372
If it were just a magazine article,
only the people who read it would know.

283
00:15:15,456 --> 00:15:16,457
But now,

284
00:15:16,540 --> 00:15:21,545
follow-up articles keep popping up online,
and the fire keeps spreading.

285
00:15:21,629 --> 00:15:24,381
Hey, you're the number one
trending topic today.

286
00:15:24,465 --> 00:15:25,883
Damn it!

287
00:15:25,966 --> 00:15:29,511
Seriously, the <i>Weekly</i><i>Shuubun</i>
and the public. What are they doing?

288
00:15:30,346 --> 00:15:32,181
What's wrong with them?

289
00:15:32,848 --> 00:15:34,683
If you've got something to say,

290
00:15:35,476 --> 00:15:37,394
say it to my face!

291
00:15:37,478 --> 00:15:39,980
There it is! The classic Jin Ichijo style!

292
00:15:40,064 --> 00:15:41,357
Listen up.

293
00:15:41,941 --> 00:15:43,776
I didn't do it.

294
00:15:43,859 --> 00:15:45,861
I did not have an affair.

295
00:15:45,945 --> 00:15:49,198
That article is a complete lie.

296
00:15:49,281 --> 00:15:52,952
Then what are those photos?

297
00:15:53,744 --> 00:15:54,912
Those are,

298
00:15:56,163 --> 00:15:57,498
in other words,

299
00:15:58,832 --> 00:16:00,376
a man and a woman.

300
00:16:05,756 --> 00:16:06,757
I can't hear you.

301
00:16:06,840 --> 00:16:09,718
But look, the photos are crystal clear.

302
00:16:09,802 --> 00:16:12,262
You can't really make excuses for this.

303
00:16:12,346 --> 00:16:14,974
In this one, you two
are embracing each other.

304
00:16:15,057 --> 00:16:17,393
If you didn't do it, is it photoshopped?

305
00:16:17,476 --> 00:16:19,019
Oh, AI?

306
00:16:19,770 --> 00:16:21,772
- Something smells good.
- What?

307
00:16:22,856 --> 00:16:24,775
The rainbow trout is ready.

308
00:16:24,858 --> 00:16:26,276
What? Already?

309
00:16:26,860 --> 00:16:28,445
I have to get the plates ready.

310
00:16:28,529 --> 00:16:29,613
Hey, wait…

311
00:16:29,697 --> 00:16:31,907
Yay, rainbow trout!

312
00:16:31,991 --> 00:16:34,743
Hold on a second.
I'm not finished talking.

313
00:16:34,827 --> 00:16:37,997
Hey! It's totally catching fire!
What do we do?

314
00:16:40,833 --> 00:16:42,251
- They're on fire!
- Oh, it's hot.

315
00:16:43,210 --> 00:16:44,420
I'm sorry.

316
00:16:44,503 --> 00:16:45,754
It seems like

317
00:16:45,838 --> 00:16:50,009
the fire over there requires a bit
more urgent attention than your fire.

318
00:16:50,092 --> 00:16:51,635
Are you okay?

319
00:16:54,096 --> 00:16:55,222
Yeah…

320
00:16:56,223 --> 00:17:00,060
Nobody ever actually listens
to what I have to say.

321
00:17:00,978 --> 00:17:02,980
I believe you, Mr. Jin.

322
00:17:03,063 --> 00:17:04,064
Midori!

323
00:17:04,148 --> 00:17:06,567
We siblings are going to support Mr. Jin!

324
00:17:06,650 --> 00:17:08,736
Wait, support?

325
00:17:10,654 --> 00:17:12,031
Your sister…

326
00:17:12,656 --> 00:17:13,949
Midori, was it?

327
00:17:14,533 --> 00:17:15,993
Oh, yes.

328
00:17:16,827 --> 00:17:20,664
I'm sorry for completely ruining
your vacation.

329
00:17:22,791 --> 00:17:24,084
But, please…

330
00:17:25,044 --> 00:17:26,795
Believe me.

331
00:17:41,351 --> 00:17:43,854
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

332
00:17:43,937 --> 00:17:47,483
You haven't happened to see
Jin Ichijo around here, have you?

333
00:17:49,860 --> 00:17:51,904
- Jin Ichijo?
- Yes.

334
00:17:52,696 --> 00:17:54,615
Oh, I am…

335
00:17:59,411 --> 00:18:00,996
with this publication.

336
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:02,706
HARUFUMI MASUDA
WEEKLY SHUUBUN

337
00:18:32,528 --> 00:18:34,321
<i>A vacation, huh.</i>

338
00:18:34,404 --> 00:18:35,364
<i>Jin Ichijo.</i>

339
00:18:35,447 --> 00:18:37,866
<i>Surrounded by young girls</i>
<i>on a harem vacation</i>

340
00:18:37,950 --> 00:18:39,409
<i>in the middle of a major scandal…</i>

341
00:18:39,493 --> 00:18:40,327
What a scoop.

342
00:18:40,410 --> 00:18:42,121
Just how angry is your wife?

343
00:18:42,204 --> 00:18:43,288
<i>Are you getting a divorce?</i>

344
00:18:43,372 --> 00:18:44,540
Who might you be?

345
00:18:44,623 --> 00:18:47,376
<i>My apologies for showing up unannounced.</i>

346
00:18:47,459 --> 00:18:50,712
Konta's special summer
orange sour drink is ready!

347
00:18:50,796 --> 00:18:52,172
Grovel!

348
00:18:52,714 --> 00:18:53,966
Grovel!

349
00:18:54,466 --> 00:18:57,469
Vacations are the best!

350
00:18:57,970 --> 00:18:59,012
Are you leaving already?

351
00:19:00,264 --> 00:19:02,850
You don't look like an ordinary person.

352
00:19:02,933 --> 00:19:04,309
<i>I don't look…</i>

353
00:19:05,394 --> 00:19:07,104
like a normal person?

354
00:19:07,604 --> 00:19:08,564
Subtitle translation by: Maslin F.
